@startuml
' Figure 7.5 – System sequence diagram: the assistant writing into the document
' Sprint 8 (FR-79). Sources: write_to_article in src/ai/ai.service.ts and
' pipeArticleWrite in src/ai/article-write-stream.ts (backend);
' features/ai/article-writer.ts and features/editor/ai-write-range.ts (frontend).
!include ../_style.puml
mainframe interaction SequenceDiagram In-document write
autonumber "0 :"

participant "Writer" as R
participant "Editor" as E
participant "Assistant\npanel" as P
participant "System" as A
participant "Language\nmodel" as L
participant "Database" as D

A -> D : Retrieve passages from the writer's\npublished articles, this one excluded
activate A
activate D
D --> A : Passages
deactivate D
A --> P : Step "retrieval" done, step "writing" active with the brief
activate P
A -> L : Stream the article text, with the draft, the profile,\nthe passages and any selection to replace
activate L
A --> P : data-article-start (placement: cursor or replace_selection)
P -> E : Open the range after the cursor's block,\nor over the selected blocks
activate E
E -> E : Tint the range and refuse the writer's own edits inside it

loop while the model streams Markdown
  L --> A : Text
  A --> P : data-article-delta
  P -> E : Insert each block once a blank line closes it,\noutside the undo history
end
L --> A : End of stream
deactivate L
A --> P : data-article-done, with the words and the headings
A --> P : Step "writing" done, "N words, M sections"
deactivate A
P --> R : Show Keep and Discard

alt the writer keeps the text
  R -> P : Keep
  P -> E : Replace the range with its final content as ONE undo step,\nthen release it
else the writer discards it
  R -> P : Discard
  P -> E : Remove the range and restore the replaced blocks\nwhere they were
end
E --> R : An ordinary, editable document
deactivate E
deactivate P

note over R, D
  The range always opens at a block boundary, never inside the writer's
  paragraph, so every node the writer owns stays byte-identical and Discard
  restores the document exactly. A selection is widened to whole blocks
  before it is sent. Only after Keep can one Ctrl+Z undo the whole write.
end note
@enduml
